{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786504425,"nonce":"YbM2bcfeMUNK/mhonqf4Cyjhf/8=","title":"Nine `guide()` closures compute the number an operator types into a tuning knob, and not one of them has a test","was":"**What is wrong.** `web/src/features/settings/tuningCopy.ts` defines **9 `guide()` closures** — one each for `refire_grace_s` (`:370`), `group_close_delay_s` (`:421`), `resolve_grace_s` (`:461`), `flap_threshold` (`:493`), `flap_window_s` (`:538`), `flap_digest_interval_s` (`:585`), `storm_window_s` (`:648`), `storm_cooldown_s` (`:689`) and `unacked_reminder_after_s` (`:726`). Each one does arithmetic over the operator's own Alertmanager timings and returns a verdict plus, at **14 sites**, a `suggest` number. That number is not advice the operator reads and weighs: `TuningSection.tsx:1614-1626` renders it as a `use {N}` button whose `onClick` writes it straight into the field. **There is no `tuningCopy.test.ts` and no `TuningSection.test.tsx`.** Zero of the nine are tested."}]}